    "question_text": "Let $a=3 \\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\frac{1}{5^{1 / 6} \\sqrt{6}}$. If $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}$ are such that\n$\\begin{gathered}3 x+2 y=\\log _a(18)^{\\frac{5}{4}} \\\\2 x-y=\\log _b(\\sqrt{1080})\\end{gathered}$\nand then $4 x+5 y$ is equal to . ________.",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [],
    "correct_answer": 8,
    "solution_text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 3 x+2 y=\\log _{3 \\sqrt{2}}(3 \\sqrt{2})^{\\frac{5}{2}}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad 6 x+4 y=5 \\quad \\ldots \\ldots(1)\\end{aligned}$\n$2 x-y=\\log _{\\frac{1}{5^{1 / 6} \\sqrt{6}}}\\left(5^{\\frac{1}{6}} \\sqrt{6}\\right)^3=-3$\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\\Rightarrow & 2 x-y=-3 \\quad.....(2)\\\\ & \\text { equation (1) }-(2) \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\quad & 4 x+5 y=8\\end{array}$",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Logarithm"
