    "held_on": "2011-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
    "question_text": "Let $\\left(x_0, y_0\\right)$ be the solution of the following equations $(2 x)^{\\log 2}=(3 y)^{\\log 3}$, $3^{\\log x}=2^{\\log y}$, then $x_0$ is equal to",
    "question_image": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "rIweA",
        "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{6}$\n",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "Lwepk",
        "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}$\n",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "QcTOM",
        "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}$\n",
        "image": null
      },
      {
        "id": "cDfc0",
        "text": "\n6",
        "image": null
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "QcTOM",
    "solution_text": "Taking log on both sides,\n$$\n\\log 2 \\cdot \\log (2 x)=\\log 3(\\log 3 y)\n$$\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\Rightarrow & \\log 2\\{\\log 2+\\log x\\} \\\\\n& =\\log 3\\{\\log 3+\\log y\\} \\\\\n\\text { and } & \\log x \\cdot \\log 3=\\log y \\log 2 \\\\\n& \\log y=\\frac{\\log x \\cdot \\log 3}{\\log 2}\n\\end{array}\n$$\nFrom Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\log 2\\{\\log 2+\\log x\\} \\\\\n&=\\log 3 \\cdot\\left\\{\\log 3+\\frac{\\log x \\cdot \\log 3}{\\log 2}\\right\\} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad(\\log 2)^2+\\log 2 \\cdot \\log x \\\\\n&=(\\log 3)^2+\\frac{(\\log 3)^2}{(\\log 2)} \\cdot \\log x \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\log x\\left\\{\\frac{(\\log 3)^2}{\\log 2}-\\log 2\\right\\} \\\\\n&=(\\log 2)^2-(\\log 3)^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\log x=-\\log 2=\\log 2^{-1} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad x=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "solution_image": null,
    "topic": "Logarithm"
  }
]